---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import { CONTACT_LINKS, SITE } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  path="/privacy/"
  title="Privacy"
  description="What the BikeTourFrance.net website does and does not collect, and how email you send to John is handled."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">This page describes what this website does today. Last updated October 2, 2026.</p>
      <ReviewNote />

      <h2>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        This website has no sign-up form, no account system, and no analytics or advertising tools. It does
        not set cookies of its own. See the <a href="/cookies/">Cookies page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>When you email John</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to <a href={CONTACT_LINKS.general}>{SITE.email}</a>, John receives your message and your
        email address in his BikeTourFrance.net email account. He uses them to reply to you. Nothing in this
        website's code sends your message anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
      <p>
        Web servers normally record technical details of each visit, such as the page requested and the
        visitor's IP address. This website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which handles those records. John
        does not receive a copy of them through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>Other sites and media</h2>
      <p>
        The Resources page loads audio files from BikeTourFrance.net's media storage only when you press play.
        It also links to Google Docs and Google Sheets and to other websites. Those sites have their own
        privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={CONTACT_LINKS.general}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
